 ms over a 10,000-ticket store' — as 'measured in docs/adr/0122-similar-ticket-retrieval.md', but that figure (and any millisecond timing) does not appear in the ADR. The ADR discusses cold-start only qualitatively ('a cold start is just the case where every ticket is missing').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f25b5837e86cf101b","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The fix', cost paragraph","norm_id":"n928986e812f39e68","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader checking the cited cost against the ADR to validate the version-bump-as-migration decision finds no such measurement"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the inserted key travels from `_reindex` to `_apply`'s `dirstate` INSERT (e.g. `_reindex` returns the key it inserted under), since `_reindex` currently returns only an int and `_apply` is where the `dirstate` row is written.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"`dirstate` gains a `ticket_id` column holding the key `_reindex` inserted under.\"","`_reindex` signature is `-> int` and computes `doc = _document(...)` then `doc[0]` locally (catchup.py:169-184)","`_apply` writes the dirstate row at catchup.py:205-210, out of scope of `_reindex`'s internal `doc[0]`"],"finding":"The plan specifies that `dirstate` records the key `_reindex` inserted under, but does not specify the data-flow by which that key reaches `_apply`'s `dirstate` INSERT. `_reindex` currently returns an int (1/0) and computes `doc[0]` only internally; recovering the key requires changing `_reindex`'s return (or recomputing `doc[0]` in `_apply`, which the dirstate-carries-the-key design exists to avoid).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0a853f15328d742e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The fix: dirstate carries the key docs was written under'; catchup.py:169-184, 201-210","norm_id":"n70bfaf2d4ee5dd05","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer must decide whether _reindex returns the key or _apply recomputes it; the plan leaves this open"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change `_reindex` to return the key it inserted under (or `None` when no row was inserted) and have `_apply` persist that into `dirstate.ticket_id`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify what `dirstate.ticket_id` records when `_reindex` is skipped (hash unchanged) or inserts nothing (`doc is None`), so the removal-path delete always carries the key the surviving `docs` row (if any) was written under.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`_apply` runs the `dirstate` INSERT unconditionally for each changed dir: `if previous is None or previous[1] != dir_hash: indexed += _reindex(...)` then always `conn.execute('INSERT INTO dirstate ...')` (catchup.py:203-210)","`_reindex` returns 0 without inserting when `doc is None` (catchup.py:178-179)"],"finding":"`_apply` writes a `dirstate` row for every `changed` directory, including the hash-unchanged path where `_reindex` is NOT called and the `doc is None` path where no `docs` row is inserted. The plan's formulation 'the key _reindex inserted under' does not specify what `ticket_id` value `dirstate` records in cycles where `_reindex` did not insert a row, so a later removal could delete `docs` under a stale, empty, or missing key.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffd133653fcab2ecf","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The fix'; catchup.py:201-210 (dirstate INSERT runs regardless of _reindex), 178-179 (doc is None early-return)","norm_id":"nb558cef6dff5ff46","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A touched-but-identical directory (mtime moved, hash unchanged) rewrites dirstate but never calls _reindex — what ticket_id is recorded?","A directory whose state will not reduce (doc is None) records a dirstate row with no corresponding docs row"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"On the hash-unchanged path, preserve the prior row's `ticket_id`; when `doc is None`, record `dir_name` (no docs row exists, so the union delete is still correct).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate every edit site for the new dirstate.ticket_id column: _ensure_schema CREATE TABLE (index.py:76-81), _reindex returning the inserted key, the _apply dirstate INSERT (catchup.py:206), and the catch_up SELECT/unpack (catchup.py:224) — and correct 'the key _reindex inserted under' since _reindex does not write dirstate.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.432,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'dirstate gains a ticket_id column holding the key _reindex inserted under'","catchup.py: _reindex (169-184) writes only to docs; the INSERT INTO dirstate is in _apply at line 206","catch_up builds `stored` from `SELECT dir_name, dir_mtime_ns, dir_hash FROM dirstate` (line 224) as (mtime, hash) tuples — adding a column touches this unpacking","index.py:76-81 _ensure_schema CREATE TABLE dirstate defines the current 3 columns"],"finding":"The plan says 'dirstate gains a ticket_id column holding the key _reindex inserted under' and that _apply reads it 'then deletes docs under the same key set _reindex uses', but _reindex does not write dirstate — the INSERT INTO dirstate is in _apply (catchup.py:206), and doc[0] is only in scope inside _reindex (invoked at line 204). The edit set to make this work is not enumerated: _ensure_schema's CREATE TABLE dirstate (index.py:76-81) must gain the column, _reindex must return/surface the key to its caller, and _apply's dirstate INSERT (line 206) plus the stored-map SELECT (line 224, which currently unpacks only (mtime, hash)) must carry it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb6bf72dc75332fd2","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The fix'; src/rebar/similar/catchup.py:169-215 and src/rebar/similar/index.py:76-81","norm_id":"n09baada8bd546b99","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds the column to _ensure_schema but discovers doc[0] is unavailable at the dirstate write site, or the SELECT at line 224 silently ignores the new column."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none"